update public.moo_versions set body_md = body_md || E'| Apply risk screening to investment proposals  | C               | A/R through planning process | R/C technical review       | R proposal owner                   | C                           | Budget/LFC/approving body         |\n| Prepare contingency plans                     | A/R coordinator | C                            | R/C                        | R hazard/sector lead               | R local plan/action         | Approval per local issuance       |\n| Prepare PSCP                                  | R/C coordinator | C                            | C                          | A/R by department for own services | I/C where service interface | Mayor/City Administrator approval |\n| Prepare and approve BDRRMP                    | C/support       | I/C                          | I                          | C                                  | A/R under applicable law    | DILG technical guidance           |\n| Monitor ecosystem risk-reduction assets       | C               | C                            | I                          | A/R CENRO/DENR                     | C                           | I                                 |\n| Review plan performance and corrective action | R/consolidates  | R for planning integration   | R for regulatory actions   | R for own actions                  | R for own plans             | CDRRMC oversight                  |\n\n# 3.19 Performance monitoring, records and corrective action\n\n| **Performance area**   | **Indicator / evidence**                                                                                                               | **Owner / review**                                           |\n|------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Risk data currency     | Share of priority datasets with complete metadata, current source version and assigned custodian; version register                     | CDRRMO GIS/data custodian; quarterly review                  |\n| Hazard map quality     | Priority hazard maps with signed validation, stated scale/use and publication metadata                                                 | CDRRMO and relevant technical office; annual/material update |\n| CDRA completeness      | Approved CDRA package; hazard coverage; exposure database completeness; MDAs; technical validation; correction of Naval/Biliran labels | CPDO/CDRA TWG; at each update                                |\n| Planning mainstreaming | CDRA MDAs cross-referenced to CLUP/CDP/LCCAP/LDIP/AIP and documented zoning/investment decisions                                       | CPDO/LDC; annual planning cycle                              |\n| Contingency readiness  | Priority hazards with approved plans, current contact/resource annexes and exercise/corrective-action records                          | CDRRMO and hazard leads; annual/exercise cycle               |\n| Service continuity     | Departments with completed essential-function inventories, BIAs, continuity strategies and tested plans                                | Continuity executive; annual review                          |\n| Barangay planning      | Verified barangay denominator; plans received, quality-reviewed, approved, tested and updated                                          | CDRRMO / DILG; quarterly status                              |\n| Inclusion              | Plans with documented consultation and accessible arrangements; unresolved barriers and corrective actions                             | Sector offices / CDRRMO; annual and post-event               |\n| Ecosystem assets       | Priority ecosystem assets with baseline condition, indicator, monitoring report and action owner                                       | CENRO/DENR; annual monitoring                                |\n\nThe CDRRMO shall consolidate evidence but shall not certify another office''s technical or statutory performance without that office''s validation. Each corrective action shall identify the finding, root cause, action, accountable owner, due date, resource implication, verification evidence and closure decision. Repeated non-closure shall be escalated through the CDRRMC and the appropriate executive or planning mechanism.\n\n# 3.20 Priority implementation and validation agenda\n\n| **Priority**                        | **Required action**                                                                                                                                                                       | **Lead / supporting offices**                                     | **Evidence of completion**                                   |\n|-------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------|\n| P1 – Data and methodology integrity | Obtain signed DHSUD MC 2025-004 and current CDRA tools; secure current OCD contingency and PSCP manuals; reconcile IAT version metadata and workbook score/status conflicts               | CDRRMO; CPDO; CLO; OCD VIII; DHSUD as needed                      | Controlled source register; resolved version and scoring log |\n| P1 – CDRA completion                | Correct Naval/Biliran labels; validate existing flood/landslide/storm-surge data; scope and complete earthquake, liquefaction, tsunami and other priority hazard assessments as justified | CPDO/CDRA TWG; CDRRMO; PHIVOLCS; MGB; PAGASA; sector offices      | Validated CDRA package and MDA register                      |\n| P1 – Barangay denominator           | Resolve 85 versus 110 using official master list and document geographic coverage                                                                                                         | CPDO; City Secretary; DILG City LGOO                              | Signed barangay master list                                  |\n| P1 – PSCP                           | Designate continuity executive; inventory essential functions; complete BIA and dependencies; prepare, approve and test PSCP                                                              | Mayor/City Administrator; all departments; HRMO; ICT; CDRRMO      | Approved PSCP, BIA and exercise report                       |\n| P1 – Contingency plans              | Confirm priority hazard scenarios; complete missing hazard-specific plans; exercise and close corrective actions                                                                          | CDRRMO; hazard technical agencies; IMT/sector leads; barangays    | Approved plans and exercise records                          |\n| P2 – Planning mainstreaming         | Create CDRA-to-CLUP/CDP crosswalk and DRR/CCA investment screening process                                                                                                                | CPDO/LDC; Budget/LFC; Engineering/OBO/Zoning; CDRRMO              | Adopted screening form and documented planning minutes       |\n| P2 – Critical dependencies          | Convert existing facility/lifeline inventory into validated dependency maps and failure-chain scenarios                                                                                   | Asset owners; utilities; CPDO; CDRRMO                             | Validated dependency register and priority actions           |\n| P2 – Inclusion and ecosystems       | Hold documented sector validation; establish ecosystem baseline/indicators and annual monitoring                                                                                          | CSWDO; GAD; PWD/older-person/youth/IP representatives; CENRO/DENR | Consultation evidence and monitoring register                |\n\n# 3.21 Conclusion\n\nChapter 3 establishes a risk-intelligence and preparedness system that connects authoritative hazard information, method-compliant CDRA, exposure and vulnerability analysis, critical infrastructure dependencies, development planning, contingency planning, service continuity and barangay preparedness. Its central control is traceability: every important risk finding must have a source, a technical owner, a decision use, a responsible office and a record showing whether the required action was completed.\n\nThe chapter is not considered implemented merely because it is approved or included in the MOO. Institutionalization requires current datasets, signed technical validation, adopted plans, completed screening records, exercised contingency and continuity arrangements, verified barangay coverage, documented corrective actions and periodic evidence-based review.\n\n# REFERENCES\n\n- Department of Human Settlements and Urban Development. (2025). Memorandum Circular No. 2025-004: Enhanced Climate and Disaster Risk Assessment (CDRA) Policy. DHSUD.\n\n- Department of Human Settlements and Urban Development. (n.d.). Climate and Disaster Risk Assessment: The 5-Step+ CDRA process. DHSUD Learning Development Repository. https://sites.google.com/dhsud.gov.ph/cdra/introduction-to-cdra/5-steps-cdra-process\n\n- Department of the Interior and Local Government. (2025). Memorandum Circular No. 2025-035: Listo si KAP. DILG.\n\n- Republic Act No. 7160. (1991). Local Government Code of 1991.\n\n- Republic Act No. 9710. (2009). Magna Carta of Women.\n\n- Republic Act No. 9729. (2009). Climate Change Act of 2009, as amended by Republic Act No. 10174.\n\n- Republic Act No. 10121. (2010). Philippine Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Act of 2010. https://www.lawphil.net/statutes/repacts/ra2010/ra_10121_2010.html\n\n- Republic Act No. 10173. (2012). Data Privacy Act of 2012.\n\n- Republic Act No. 10821. (2016). Children''s Emergency Relief and Protection Act.\n\n- Republic Act No. 12076. (2024). Ligtas Pinoy Centers Act.\n\n- United Nations Office for Disaster Risk Reduction. (2015). Sendai Framework for Disaster Risk Reduction 2015–2030.\n\n- United Nations Office for Disaster Risk Reduction. (2017). Disaster Resilience Scorecard for Cities: Detailed Level Assessment.\n\nProject source documents used: Ormoc CDRRMO–EOC MOO Chapter 1 Consolidated (October 2026 working draft); Chapter 2 Enhanced Integrated Draft; Ormoc CDRRMO–EOC Institutional Assessment Tool v1.3 workbook (nine sheets). The workbook''s Guide/Crosswalk version references v1.1 in places; the instrument version history requires reconciliation before the assessment is treated as a controlled baseline.\n\nSource limitations: The full Ormoc CDRA report, Complete CLUP PDF, signed LDRRMP, current OCD contingency-planning manual, and PSCP Guidebook were not present among the files retrieved for this rebuild. Findings attributed to these documents are therefore limited to what is explicitly recorded in the IAT and Chapter 1 project materials. The City must attach and verify the original source documents before final technical adoption.\n'
